        "thinking": "The user is asking whether the Cloudflare deployment should now work exactly the same as the regular Node.js deployment. Let me think about this honestly.\n\nThe answer is: mostly yes, but with a few exceptions that are inherent to the CF Workers environment:\n\n1. **What works the same**: All the DB-backed API routes (companies, agents, assets, projects, issues, environments, routines, goals, approvals, secrets, costs, activity, dashboard, user profiles, sidebar, access/members/invites/join-requests, auth, CLI auth, admin users, etc.)\n\n2. **What doesn't work or works differently**:\n   - **Adapters**: Returns empty array (no adapter registry in CF Workers)\n   - **Plugins**: Also returns empty array (no plugin registry in CF Workers)\n   - **Company skills and skill browsing**: Will fail because they need to read local files from the filesystem, which CF Workers can't do\n   - **Invite test-resolution**: Will fail with DNS unavailable error\n   - **Database backups**: Returns 501 (no backup service)\n   - **WebSocket events**: Accepts the WS connection but won't send any server-sent events since there's no pub/sub bus\n   - **Agent task execution**: Still limited without Durable Objects properly wired up\n   - **File uploads**: Uses R2 instead of local filesystem\n\nSo the behavior isn't actually identical across both environments. I need to be more precise about what will and won't work.",
